// A sorted index whose entities share keys: made again in place and
// anew, its rows always in the order a `for ... by` gives (those of a
// key in the order they are stored), on one core and on many. (Before
// 2026-10-23, made in place, those of a key stayed in the order they had
// in it: 600 of 30,000 rows where the `for` has them.)
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/index_ties.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/index_ties.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.one

// CHECK:      frame 0: 30000 of 30000 rows as `by` has them, 30000 visited
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 1: [[N1:[0-9]+]] of [[N1]] rows as `by` has them, [[N1]] visited
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 2: [[N2:[0-9]+]] of [[N2]] rows as `by` has them, [[N2]] visited
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 3: [[N3:[0-9]+]] of [[N3]] rows as `by` has them, [[N3]] visited
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 4: [[N4:[0-9]+]] of [[N4]] rows as `by` has them, [[N4]] visited
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 5: [[N5:[0-9]+]] of [[N5]] rows as `by` has them, [[N5]] visited
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 6: [[N6:[0-9]+]] of [[N6]] rows as `by` has them, [[N6]] visited
